From 6b346c5f81f55baf5bb84af37a95c612a18d4fe3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:48:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Views on the data of a material: FieldView and
 MaterialDataView

FieldView describes the values of a group of variables at a set of points
with two strides (point by point, component by component, uniform values,
padding), checked as the views of mgis::function. MaterialDataView describes
the data of a material stored in arrays owned by the calling code. All the
functions on batches exist on views, with the overloads of the functions on
material data managers; the overloads taking a workspace process a behaviour
generated by the generic interface point by point, gathering the values of a
point whose components are not contiguous. The functions on material data
managers call the functions on views (make_view), with temporary arrays on
the stack. The workspace knows its behaviour and holds the local arrays of a
point.
